From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:37:13 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: datapath: clear the subif's netif on deregister

dp_deregister_subif_private() resets the subif slot it is releasing --
it zeroes the mib and the flags -- but leaves subif_info[i].netif
pointing at the net_device that has just been deregistered. AVM's 08.25
GPL release adds "sif->netif = NULL;" beside the flags reset
(datapath_api.c:905 in Linux 4.9.337); 07.30, which we were transcribed
from, does not. Take it.

This is hygiene, not a use-after-free, and the difference matters enough
to spell out. Nothing in this tree dereferences that pointer. The only
reads of subif_info[].netif anywhere are the comparison at :961 that
guards this very function ("if (port_info->subif_info[i].netif != dev)")
and the %p in the dev_err beside it -- both upstream of the reset block,
both in the same call. Neither of the two scans over subif_info[] keys
on netif: :745 keys on flags, :940 on subif. We have no
dp_get_port_subitf_via_dev and no dp_lan_wan_bridging, which is where
AVM's framework does look a netdev up this way. RX resolves its delivery
netdev through a different table entirely, g_cbm_rx_netdev[]
(cqm/grx500/cbm_intr.c:286) via cbm_rx_resolve_netdev() -- and that one
is already cleared on the way down, in intel_xrx500's ndo_stop.

What the assignment buys is that a second deregister of the same slot now
fails the :961 device-match guard instead of passing it, so a
double-deregister is caught rather than silently repeating the teardown. It
costs one store on a path that already does a memset.

The comment over the block claimed the reset covered "mib / flags /
device_name". device_name was never cleared here, and AVM does not clear
it either; it is written once at :801 and no code in the tree reads it
back. So the comment now names what is actually reset and says why
device_name is left alone, rather than describing a store that does not
exist.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/datapath/datapath_api.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/datapath/datapath_api.c
index 637a79496c22..562261a33b9a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/datapath/datapath_api.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/datapath/datapath_api.c
@@ -757,10 +757,10 @@ static int dp_deregister_subif_private(int inst, struct module *owner,
 	cqm_port = port_info->subif_info[i].cqm_deq_port;
 	bp = port_info->subif_info[i].bp;
 
-	/* (4) AVM:720-724 — reset per-subif mib / flags / device_name. */
 	memset(&port_info->subif_info[i].mib, 0,
 	       sizeof(port_info->subif_info[i].mib));
 	port_info->subif_info[i].flags = 0;
+	port_info->subif_info[i].netif = NULL;
 	port_info->num_subif--;
 
 	/* (5) AVM:725-730 — subif_platform_set unprograms CTP / BridgePort
